From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hid_device: accept the boot keyboard's one-byte output report

In the boot protocol a keyboard's output report is one byte, its LEDs, but
the size check asked every keyboard report for at least eight bytes, so a
host's Caps Lock or Num Lock in boot protocol was dropped on the interrupt
channel and refused on SET_REPORT. Input reports still need eight. Upstream
master has the same check.

diff --git a/src/classic/hid_device.c b/src/classic/hid_device.c
--- a/src/classic/hid_device.c
+++ b/src/classic/hid_device.c
@@ -343,7 +343,8 @@
     if (hid_device_in_boot_protocol_mode(cid)){
         switch (report_id){
             case HID_BOOT_MODE_KEYBOARD_ID:
-                if (report_size < 8) return 0;
+                // the boot keyboard's output report is one byte, its LEDs
+                if (report_size < ((report_type == HID_REPORT_TYPE_OUTPUT) ? 1 : 8)) return 0;
                 break;
             case HID_BOOT_MODE_MOUSE_ID:
                 if (report_size < 1) return 0;
